## RDM person identifiers

The reporting data mart uses several "user" identifier columns that overlap but serve different purposes:

| Column name | Meaning | When to use |
|---|---|---|
| `personuser_id` | Unique instance of a UserId + Email within a Space. The true primary key of the `person` table. | Primary key for `person` table |
| `person_user_id` / `editor_person_user_id` / `author_person_user_id` / `editorial_board_member_person_user_id` | Person-level ID derived from `personuser_id`. Appears across most RDM tables as a foreign key. | **Primary join key across RDM tables** — use this to link person → author → editor → editorial_board_member |
| `person_id` | Derived person entity ID. Many `personuser_id`s can map to one `person_id` (M:1). Represents the "first" `person_id` where there are multiple primary emails or non-null H-index values. **Maps directly to `AuthorId` in AIRAK** (verified 100% match). | For cross-system joins to AIRAK; also used in RT editor workflows |
| `user_id` / `editor_user_id` / `author_user_id` | Registered user ID. **`user_id = -1` means a non-registered user.** | For joining to `user_metrics` |
| `author_id` | **Not a person-level ID.** Unique instance of JournalRole + Taxonomy + User/Email + Space. One person can have multiple `author_id`s. | Primary key on `author` table only — do not use to identify a person across tables |
| `journal_user_id` | Journal-specific user ID | Less commonly used for cross-table joins |
| `space_id` | Logical data separation (Frontiers vs shared-service tenants). **`space_id = 0` means missing space.** | Filter or group by tenant |

**Common RDM join patterns:**

```sql
-- Person to their editorial board memberships
FROM reporting_data_mart.person p
JOIN reporting_data_mart.editorial_board_member ebm
  ON p.person_user_id = ebm.editorial_board_member_person_user_id

-- Article to its authors
FROM reporting_data_mart.article art
JOIN reporting_data_mart.author a
  ON art.article_id = a.author_article_id

-- Person to user activity metrics
FROM reporting_data_mart.person p
JOIN reporting_data_mart.user_metrics um
  ON p.person_user_id = um.user_id

-- Research topic to its host editor
FROM reporting_data_mart.research_topic rt
JOIN reporting_data_mart.research_topic_editor rte
  ON rt.research_topic_id = rte.editor_research_topic_id
WHERE rte.editor_order = 1  -- host editor only
```

