## Data quality known issues

| Issue | Source | Detail |
|---|---|---|
| DOI casing | AIRAK + RDM | DOIs are stored in mixed case. **Always use `LOWER()` on both sides** of DOI joins |
| Dimensions download/view bot activity | Dimensions | Bot activity affects download counts, particularly through 2024. Treat download metrics with caution; views were going down while downloads spiked |
| Salesforce Task call/email distinction | Salesforce | The field distinguishing calls from emails is unreliable — calls are manually logged and under-reported |
| RT contributor–article linking | RTM/Salesforce | ~5% of confirmed contributors who submit are not linked to their profile (possible disambiguation issue) |
| Organisation hierarchy inconsistency | AIRAK/RDM | Sub-institutions may not roll up consistently (e.g. "University College London" vs "University of London"). Use `OrganizationTopParent` to normalise |
| EarlyFoS vs OpenAlex FoS | AIRAK vs EarlyFoS | EarlyFoS scores are internally consistent but **not identical** to OpenAlex. They can be used as an alternative at submission time |
| Author retraction data | AIRAK | `RetractedPublicationCount` may not capture all retractions; cross-reference with `Retraction` table and Retraction Watch |
| `JournalId = -1` | AIRAK | Some publications have `JournalId = -1` (unknown journal). Filter these out: `WHERE JournalId > -1` |
| Organisation affiliation mismatch | RDM vs AIRAK | Loop takes priority over AIRAK for primary org/email. `reporting_data_mart.person` may show a different org than `airak.AuthorOrganization` for the same person |
| `HierarchyId` not persistent | AIRAK | `OrganizationHierarchy.HierarchyId` is regenerated and **not stable across loads** — do not use as a tracking key |
| RT contributor counts differ across platforms | RTM/SF/Tableau | Known discrepancy — Tableau typically lower, SF may miss non-RTM invitations |
| `author_id` is not person-level | RDM | `author_id` is a unique instance of Role+Taxonomy+User+Space. One person can have multiple `author_id`s. Use `author_person_user_id` to identify the person |
| `user_id = -1` | RDM | Indicates a non-registered user |
| `space_id = 0` | RDM | Indicates a missing space |

